<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Castro Urdiales</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Castro Urdiales is a port town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-biscay">Bay of Biscay</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabria">Cantabria</a>, in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. It is identified with the Roman colony of Flaviobriga, founded under Vespasian in the territory of the Autrigones. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was an important fishing and trading port of the Hermandad de las Marismas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/castro-urdiales.jpg" alt="Castro Urdiales" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Asqueladd · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castro_Urdiales._Cantabria.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
